---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/ui/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/schema';
import { smsHref, phoneDisplay } from '../lib/text-cta';
const sms = smsHref(Astro.url.pathname);

const lastUpdated = '2026-10-05';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy · Winters Code"
  description="What this site collects, why it collects it, and how it is kept safe. Plain English, no tracking pixels, no data sales, and no surprises."
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumbSchema([
      { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
      { name: 'Privacy', path: '/privacy' },
    ]))} />
  </Fragment>

  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy', path: '/privacy' }]} />

  <article class="legal-page">
    <div class="legal-eyebrow mono">LEGAL · PRIVACY POLICY</div>
    <h1 class="h1 legal-h1">Privacy, in plain English.</h1>
    <p class="legal-tagline">
      I built this site because I was tired of small businesses getting fleeced by software
      they didn't ask for. So I'm not going to do that to you either.
    </p>
    <p class="small legal-updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="legal-body">
      <p class="legal-lead">
        Short version: I collect what you give me, I use it to do the work you hired me for,
        I don't sell it, I don't track you across the web, and I delete it if you ask.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2 legal-h2">What I collect</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>When you contact me:</strong> name, email, phone if you share it, business name,
        city, industry, project type, and whatever you write in the brief. Stored with it: the
        IP address, country and referring page the request came from, which the site uses to
        keep spam out. A text or a call reaches my phone like any other.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>When you visit the site:</strong> Cloudflare (my host) logs standard server stuff
        like IP address, browser, and referrer. No Google Analytics. No Facebook Pixel. No
        advertising trackers. No cross-site cookies.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2 legal-h2">What this site loads, and where your words go</h2>
      <ul class="legal-list">
        <li><strong>Every page:</strong> Cloudflare hosts it, and Cloudflare Web Analytics counts page
          views with a small script from static.cloudflareinsights.com. It sets no cookies.</li>
        <li><strong>The brief form on /contact:</strong> Cloudflare Turnstile, from
          challenges.cloudflare.com, checks for spam. A brief you send is stored in my Cloudflare
          account and a copy is emailed to me.</li>
        <li><strong>The free audit on /audit:</strong> the address you enter goes from my server to
          Google PageSpeed Insights and Mozilla Observatory, which score it. Results are kept for six
          hours so a repeat check is quick, and your IP address counts toward a daily limit.</li>
        <li><strong>The MyKonos chat demo:</strong> what you type, and your IP address for its five
          messages a day, goes to my own server, which runs it through an AI model provider.</li>
        <li><strong>Cal.com, email and text:</strong> those open only when you tap them.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="h2 legal-h2">What I do with it</h2>
      <p>
        I answer your message, scope your project, prepare a quote, deliver the work, and
        keep in touch on active builds. That's the whole list. I don't sell, rent, share,
        or trade client information with marketing companies, data brokers, or anyone else.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2 legal-h2">Where it lives</h2>
      <p>
        Client emails sit in standard business inboxes. Project code sits in private GitHub
        repos I control. Anything I build for you that handles your customers' data uses
        encryption in transit (HTTPS), row-level security on the database, and patched
        dependencies. I treat your data like I'd want mine treated.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2 legal-h2">Third parties I rely on</h2>
      <p>
        Cloudflare hosts the site and DNS, checks forms for spam and counts page views. Supabase or similar managed backends
        run client apps when contracted. Google and Mozilla score the sites people run through
        the audit. Each one has its own privacy policy.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2 legal-h2">Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:preston@winterscode.com">preston@winterscode.com</a> and ask
        for any of these:
      </p>
      <ul class="legal-list">
        <li>A copy of what I have on you</li>
        <li>Corrections to anything that's wrong</li>
        <li>Full deletion, no questions asked</li>
        <li>To opt out of any future contact from me</li>
      </ul>
      <p>I'll honor it within a week. Usually same-day.</p>

      <h2 class="h2 legal-h2">Children</h2>
      <p>
        This is a business-to-business service. Nothing here is aimed at children under 13,
        and I don't knowingly collect information from minors.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2 legal-h2">When this changes</h2>
      <p>
        If I update this policy in any meaningful way, the date at the top moves and the
        change shows up in the site's public git history (<a href="/changelog">/changelog</a>).
        Everything is on the record.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2 legal-h2">Questions</h2>
      <p>
        I'm a person. Text <a href={sms}>{phoneDisplay}</a> and it reaches me directly, or email
        <a href="mailto:preston@winterscode.com">preston@winterscode.com</a>. Or just stop me
        on the street in Bandon.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 48px 4px 64px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 740px) {
    .legal-page {
      padding: 64px 4px 80px;
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .legal-page {
      padding: 80px 0 96px;
    }
  }

  .legal-eyebrow {
    color: var(--color-copper);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 740px) {
    .legal-eyebrow { font-size: 12px; }
  }

  .legal-h1 {
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }

  .legal-tagline {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 17px;
    color: var(--color-ash-300);
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    max-width: 600px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .legal-tagline { font-size: 19px; }
  }

  .legal-updated {
    margin-top: 8px;
    color: var(--color-ash-500);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }

  .legal-body {
    margin-top: 36px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 18px;
    color: var(--color-ash-300);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .legal-body { font-size: 16px; }
  }
  .legal-body p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .legal-lead {
    padding: 16px 18px;
    background: rgba(77, 216, 168, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid rgba(77, 216, 168, 0.25);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    color: var(--color-ash-100);
    font-style: italic;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 16px !important;
    line-height: 1.6 !important;
  }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .legal-lead {
      font-size: 18px !important;
      padding: 20px 24px;
    }
  }

  .legal-h2 {
    margin-top: 24px;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 740px) {
    .legal-h2 { margin-top: 28px; }
  }

  .legal-body strong {
    color: var(--color-ash-100);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .legal-body a {
    color: var(--color-copper-bright);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--copper-hairline);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  @media (hover: hover) {

    .legal-body a:hover {
    color: var(--color-wc-green);
    text-decoration-color: var(--color-wc-green-dim);
  }}

  .legal-list {
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
  }
  .legal-list li {
    padding-left: 18px;
    position: relative;
  }
  .legal-list li::before {
    content: '·';
    position: absolute;
    left: 4px;
    top: 0;
    color: var(--color-copper);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
</style>
